### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Kong Identity workshop — live API walkthrough
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and JetBrains' built-in HTTP client.
###
### Nothing secret lives in this file. Export these in the shell that launches
### your editor (or run scripts 01–04 first, which write .generated/state.env):
###   KONNECT_TOKEN   KONNECT_REGION   DIRECTORY_ID   PRINCIPAL_ID
###   CONTROL_PLANE_ID   CONSUMER_ID   OIDC_SUBJECT   DEMO_CLIENT_SECRET
###   CG_STANDARD_ID  CG_GOLD_ID
### Run requests top to bottom; copy ids from each response into your shell env.
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@region = {{$processEnv KONNECT_REGION}}
@konnect = https://{{region}}.api.konghq.com
@token = {{$processEnv KONNECT_TOKEN}}
@directoryId = {{$processEnv DIRECTORY_ID}}
@principalId = {{$processEnv PRINCIPAL_ID}}
@controlPlaneId = {{$processEnv CONTROL_PLANE_ID}}
@consumerId = {{$processEnv CONSUMER_ID}}
@oidcIssuer = http://keycloak:8080/realms/kong-workshop
@oidcSubject = {{$processEnv OIDC_SUBJECT}}
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080
@proxy = http://localhost:8000

### ── Scenario 2 · Keycloak ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 2.1 Discovery document — the plugin reads this from the issuer URL
GET {{keycloak}}/realms/kong-workshop/.well-known/openid-configuration

### 2.2 Client Credentials grant — copy `access_token` into jwt.io (or script 01b) to read the claims
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/kong-workshop/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=workshop-demo-client&client_secret={{$processEnv DEMO_CLIENT_SECRET}}

### ── Scenario 1 · Kong Identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1.1 Does a directory already exist? (one per region per org)
GET {{konnect}}/v2/directories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 1.2 Create the directory — only if 1.1 returned an empty list
POST {{konnect}}/v2/directories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "kong-identity-directory",
  "description": "Directory for the Kong Identity workshop",
  "allow_all_control_planes": true
}

### 1.3 Create a principal, with metadata
POST {{konnect}}/v2/directories/{{directoryId}}/principals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "display_name": "workshop-demo-client",
  "description": "Machine client for the Kong Identity workshop",
  "metadata": { "business_unit": "payments", "environment": "workshop" }
}

### 1.4 Link the principal to the Keycloak client: issuer + claim must match the token exactly
POST {{konnect}}/v2/directories/{{directoryId}}/principals/{{principalId}}/identities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "oidc",
  "issuer": "{{oidcIssuer}}",
  "claim": { "name": "sub", "value": "{{oidcSubject}}" }
}

### 1.5 Verify
GET {{konnect}}/v2/directories/{{directoryId}}/principals/{{principalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{konnect}}/v2/directories/{{directoryId}}/principals/{{principalId}}/identities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── Scenario 3 · Through the gateway ──────────────────────────────────────────

### 3A No token → 401
GET {{proxy}}/anything

### 3C Valid token + matching principal → 200 (paste a fresh access_token from 2.2)
GET {{proxy}}/anything
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Datakit trace — every node's input/output (needs the datakit plugin from kong/plugins.yml)
GET {{proxy}}/anything
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
X-Datakit-Debug-Trace: true

### ── Scenario 4 · Consumer linkage ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4.3 Add a control_plane_consumer identity to the SAME principal
POST {{konnect}}/v2/directories/{{directoryId}}/principals/{{principalId}}/identities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "control_plane_consumer",
  "control_plane_id": "{{controlPlaneId}}",
  "consumer_id": "{{consumerId}}"
}

### ── Scenario 5 · Consumer Group linkage (reserved metadata key, NOT an identity) ─

### 5.3 Map the principal to a group. Send the FULL metadata object.
PATCH {{konnect}}/v2/directories/{{directoryId}}/principals/{{principalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "metadata": {
    "business_unit": "payments",
    "environment": "workshop",
    "consumer_groups": ["{{$processEnv CG_STANDARD_ID}}"]
  }
}

### 5.4 Move it to the gold group
PATCH {{konnect}}/v2/directories/{{directoryId}}/principals/{{principalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "metadata": {
    "business_unit": "payments",
    "environment": "workshop",
    "consumer_groups": ["{{$processEnv CG_GOLD_ID}}"]
  }
}
